<!--Post: 2593--><!--Time: 1103833147-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2593"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Tbear<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Tbear<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, December 23, 2004 - 12:19 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Otero Home 0.39 miles from Edgemoor Park <BR>K Bright .42 miles from Fairmont Park <BR>Vian .2 miles from Lynwood Park &#40;NE corner&#41; <BR>Fox .43 miles from Friendship Park &#40;NW corner&#41; <BR>Attempted S. Pinecrest .5 Cypress Park &#40;SW corner&#41; <BR>Wegerle .7 miles Sims Park &#40;NE Corner&#41; <BR>And of course the latest drop at Murdock Park <BR> <BR>All of these parks are decent in size. The smallest being Murdock Park @ 9.89 acres and the largest being Sim Park @ 181.48 acres, including public golf couse&#40;As per the Wichita, KS Parks and Recreations&#41; <BR>All of these parks were in existence at the times of these murders/attempted murders. <BR> <BR> <BR>And of course the latest drop-off at Murdock Park. <BR> <BR>Curious item to mention. If the City has not changed the disctict #&#39;s for these parks... <BR>Tuesday murders were near parks with even district #&#39;s. Thursday murders were near parks with odd district #&#39;s. I need to double check the attempt date. I forgot to write it down. <BR> <BR>I apologize this is sort of sloppy and thrown together, like i said i don&#39;t have a lot of time at this time of year.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 2593-->
<!--Post: 2596--><!--Time: 1103834169-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2596"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Tbear<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Tbear<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, December 23, 2004 - 12:36 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->attempt was 4/28/1979 odd, this was on a Saturday. No other know vic or attempted vic is known to have been targeted on a Saturday<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 2596-->
<!--Post: 2606--><!--Time: 1103838640-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2606"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Tbear<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Tbear<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, December 23, 2004 - 1:50 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->At any rate, here is my theory <BR>I believe BTK held a &#39;maintenance&#39; position with Parks and recreation. A coupleof things have led me to this belief, granted they are weak. <BR>1: proximity of vics to parks. Not many people can live that close to a park with out going there. &#40;especially if they have children, grandchildren,babysit, ect&#41; <BR>2: There is usually a relationship of sorts w/ p&amp;r workers and PD/Sheriffs in small to mid sized cities/towns. Hence they will use a lot of the same verbage. <BR>3: A large percentage of city workers are Vets. &#40;I am of the belief that BTK is a Vet, and I believe he was drafted, which would mean that he is not the only son of his family.&#41; <BR>4: He would be able to &#39;shop&#39; for vics and not stick out like a sore thumb. Afterall, he&#39;s supposed to be there, maintaining the park. <BR>  <BR>  <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 2606-->
<!--Post: 2610--><!--Time: 1103842122-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2610"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Q<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Q<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, December 23, 2004 - 2:48 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Take a look at the Glen Campbell Lyrics Thread, that I started. <BR> <BR><a href="http://www.catchbtk.com/discus/messages/11/204.html?1103157547" target=_top>http://www.catchbtk.com/discus/messages/11/204.htm l?1103157547</a> <BR> <BR>Note: &#34;Where&#39;s the Playground Suzie&#34; &amp; &#34;Gentle On My Mind&#34; in paticular.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 2610-->
<!--Post: 2626--><!--Time: 1103852258-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2626"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Tbear<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Tbear<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, December 23, 2004 - 5:37 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Didn&#39;t mean to step on your toes Q, I&#39;ve been thinking aboout this for few weeks and only had time to skim through alot of the theories and to do some mapping. There are some questions I have about other drops this year. I don&#39;t have time to do all the research on where the other drops were made &#40;physical address&#41;. Although I am sure he&#39;s retired by now<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 2626-->
<!--Post: 2631--><!--Time: 1103857571-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2631"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Q<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Q<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, December 23, 2004 - 7:06 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->No where near my toes Bud. I just wanted yours and others input on how creepy the simularities in the lyrics are. It ties to the &#34;parks&#34; theory &amp; BTK brought up &#34;Wichita Hangman&#34; which is an obvious ref to the Jimmy Webb/ Glen Campbell song but look at the others too. <BR> <BR>As for the toes thing... I&#39;m not one of those, I pee&#39;d on the hydrant first types I&#39;m here to share and learn and hopefully help. Some seem to be a bit control freakish, almost like they are living vicariously through him. That is sick. <BR> <BR>I&#39;m not one of those.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 2631-->
<!--Post: 6000--><!--Time: 1107476863-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6000"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Purple<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Purple<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, February 03, 2005 - 4:27 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->In the Vian case, there is a park only two blocks from her house just to the west.  Henry park is very small and has a playground.  <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6000-->
